   "published": "Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:47:02 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794440822.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "President Lee Jae Myung called for unity between the government and the ruling Democratic Party of Korea (DPK) as he held a dinner meeting with DPK leader Kim Min-seok and floor leader Han Byung-do on Wednesday, his office said. During the dinner at Cheong Wa Dae, Kim asked the government for bold and swift measures to overcome polarization and boost consumption, presidential spokesperson Kang Yu-jung said in a written briefing. Lim and Choi were among the dinner participants.",
   "summary_zh": "总统办公室表示，李在明总统周三与执政的朝鲜民主党（DPK）领导人金敏锡和院内议长韩炳-do共进晚餐时，呼吁政府与该党加强团结。总统发言人姜宇 Jung在书面简报中称，在青瓦台举行的晚宴上，金敏锡要求政府采取大胆而迅速的措施，以克服社会极化并提振消费。林某和崔某出席了晚宴。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "President Lee Jae Myung called for unity between the government and the ruling Democratic Party of Korea (DPK) as he held a dinner meeting with DPK leader Kim Min-seok and floor leader Han Byung-do on Wednesday, his office said. During the dinner at Cheong Wa Dae, Kim asked the government for bold and swift measures to overcome polarization and boost consumption, presidential spokesperson Kang Yu-jung said in a written briefing. In response, Lee stressed the need for the party and the government to \"move as one\" in order for the people's lives to improve, and asked that the party and the National Assembly extend their active support to get the government's 2027 budget proposal passed, Kang said. Lee also asked his chief of staff, Lim Kwang-hyun, and senior political affairs secretary, Choi In-ho, to closely communicate with the National Assembly at all times. Lim and Choi were among the dinner participants. Though there had been speculation Lee and the party leaders could discuss controversial issues, such as real estate taxes and a special counsel bill on alleged fabricated indictments, a presidential official said neither topic was brought up",
