   "summary": "The ruling and opposition parties have tentatively agreed on introducing taxes on digital assets in 2029, a ruling party lawmaker said Wednesday, as the government seeks to delay such taxes by two years. Rep. Oh Gi-hyoung of the ruling Democratic Party of Korea told reporters that a subcommittee of the National Assembly's finance and economy committee that includes lawmakers from the main opposition People Power Party has reached a consensus on delaying taxes on digital assets.",
   "summary_zh": "执政党议员周三表示，执政党与反对党已初步同意于2029年对数字资产征税。目前政府正寻求将征税推迟两年。执政的朝鲜民主党议员吴起镛对记者说，国会财政经济委员会下设的小组委员会已就是否推迟征收数字资产税达成共识，该委员会包括主要反对党国民力量党的议员。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The ruling and opposition parties have tentatively agreed on introducing taxes on digital assets in 2029, a ruling party lawmaker said Wednesday, as the government seeks to delay such taxes by two years. Rep. Oh Gi-hyoung of the ruling Democratic Party of Korea told reporters that a subcommittee of the National Assembly's finance and economy committee that includes lawmakers from the main opposition People Power Party has reached a consensus on delaying taxes on digital assets. Oh said the parliamentary subcommittee has discussed some procedural matters on the government's plan, hinting that the relevant bill could be approved. Last week, Finance Minister Lee Hyoung-il said the government will seek to delay a planned tax on digital assets by two years, from 2027 to 2029",
