   "_dt": 1794408723.0,
   "ageDays": 0.38,
   "summary": "Finance Minister Lee Hyoung-il on Wednesday called for South Korea's financial attaches in overseas missions to closely monitor the impact of the U.S. midterm elections on the global economy, including how individual countries are responding. \"We also need to focus on how changes in the political landscape following the U.S. midterm elections will affect the Trump administration's policy direction,\" the finance minister added, asking the attaches to closely monitor relevant developments.",
   "summary_zh": "财政部长李炯烈周三呼吁韩国驻海外使团的金融专员密切监测美国中期选举对全球经济的影响，包括各国如何回应。他补充说：“我们还需要关注美国中期选举后政治格局的变化将如何影响特朗普政府的政策方向”，并要求这些专员密切监测相关事态发展。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Finance Minister Lee Hyoung-il on Wednesday called for South Korea's financial attaches in overseas missions to closely monitor the impact of the U.S. midterm elections on the global economy, including how individual countries are responding. Lee made the remarks during his first meeting with financial attaches at 18 overseas missions since taking office in September, held virtually to review the latest economic trends in major countries, according to the Ministry of Finance and Economy. During the meeting, Lee stressed that South Korea faces external uncertainties, including fiscal instability in Europe and global geopolitical tensions, despite the country's robust exports. \"In order to turn recent achievements into sustainable growth, we need to preemptively identify changes in the external environment and take steps to address risks in advance,\" Lee said during the meeting. \"We also need to focus on how changes in the political landscape following the U.S. midterm elections will affect the Trump administration's policy direction,\" the finance minister added, asking the attaches to closely monitor relevant developments. The finance minister also called for the attaches to closely watch the fiscal crisis in France and its potential impact on the global economy, as well as global supply chains amid the Russia-Ukraine war and the U.S.-Iran war. The finance ministry said it will continue to communicate closely with the financial attaches to review economic and policy trends in major countries and proactively respond to external risks",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
