   "_dt": 1794365223.0,
   "ageDays": 0.89,
   "summary": "Korea's top economic policymaker said Wednesday the government will release annual economic growth forecasts three times a year starting in 2027, up from the current two, to respond more proactively to changing economic conditions. Finance Minister Lee Hyoung-il made the announcement as he discussed details of the government's economic growth strategy for next year with relevant ministers, indicating the plan will seek sustainable growth by addressing disparities.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国最高经济决策官员周三表示，政府将从2027年起每年发布3次年度经济增长预测，高于目前的2次，以更主动地应对不断变化的经济形势。财政部长李炯一在与相关部长讨论政府明年的经济增长战略细节时宣布了这一消息，并表示该计划将通过解决差距问题来寻求可持续增长。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korea's top economic policymaker said Wednesday the government will release annual economic growth forecasts three times a year starting in 2027, up from the current two, to respond more proactively to changing economic conditions. Finance Minister Lee Hyoung-il made the announcement as he discussed details of the government's economic growth strategy for next year with relevant ministers, indicating the plan will seek sustainable growth by addressing disparities. \"In order to promptly respond to the changing environment at home and abroad, the government will increase the number of economic outlooks issued from two to three, which would mark the first change in 32 years,\" Lee said. Lee said the government will no longer release a separate economic growth strategy for the second half of the year under the revised system, but will instead draw up supplementary measures to address economic conditions when it announces its growth forecasts. The finance minister said details will be announced in December following discussions with relevant ministries. During the meeting, Lee added that the government will continue efforts to maintain the current growth momentum through flagship initiatives, including the three megaprojects",
