   "title": "Marcos wants South China Sea code of conduct finalized during Asean",
   "url": "https://www.inquirer.net/495229/marcos-wants-south-china-sea-code-of-conduct-finalized-during-asean/",
   "domain": "inquirer.net",
   "source": "inquirer.net",
   "published": "Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:55:04 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794329704.0,
   "ageDays": 1.3,
   "summary": "READ: WPS: PH upbeat on progress in South China Sea code of conduct talks Asked whether the COC would be settled during the Asean Summit scheduled for Nov. 15 to 17, Castro said, “Alam naman natin na isa ito sa nais ng Pangulo na ma-finalize.” (We know that this is one of the things the president wants to finalize.) Castro said Marcos remains hopeful about reaching an agreement, even as the Philippines nears the end of its hosting of the Asean Summit.",
   "summary_zh": "阅读：菲律宾对南海行为准则谈判进展表示乐观。当被问及行为准则是否会在11月15日至17日举行的东盟峰会上敲定时，Castro表示：“我们知道，这是总统希望敲定的事项之一。”Castro说，即使菲律宾即将结束对东盟峰会的东道主职责，Marcos仍对达成协议抱有希望。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "At a briefing on Monday, Castro said sealing the agreement has long been one of the president’s goals, as it is intended to help de-escalate tensions in the contested waters. READ: WPS: PH upbeat on progress in South China Sea code of conduct talks Asked whether the COC would be settled during the Asean Summit scheduled for Nov. 15 to 17, Castro said, “Alam naman natin na isa ito sa nais ng Pangulo na ma-finalize.” (We know that this is one of the things the president wants to finalize.) Castro said Marcos remains hopeful about reaching an agreement, even as the Philippines nears the end of its hosting of the Asean Summit. “Ang nais ng Pangulo ay magandang makikipagrelasyon sa lahat ng bansa at kung anuman ang maaaring maging agreement para sa kapayapaan ng rehiyon, iyon ang nais ng Pangulo,” she said. The proposed Code of Conduct is intended to establish rules governing the behavior of countries in the disputed waters and prevent incidents that could lead to armed conflict. Asean and China adopted the nonbinding Declaration on the Conduct of Parties in the South China Sea in 2002, but negotiations for a more comprehensive agreement have continued for decades. In a media interview in October, Marcos noted “good progress” in the negotiations for the COC in the South China Sea. “We’re working very, very hard, we’re making good progress as a matter of fact, in terms of the code of conduct,” Marcos told Forbes Chair and editor-in-chief Steve Forbes during an onstage discussion at the 24th Forbes Global CEO Conference in Singapore. “The discussions have been going on for a while, and sometimes it’s a bit frustrating that just the definitions of ordinary words are becoming bones of contention,” he said. “But we are determined to come to an agreement and to hopefully de-escalate the situation,” he added. Your subscription could not be saved. Please try again. Your subscription has been successful. In July, Foreign Affairs Secretary Ma. Theresa Lazaro said Asean and China were aiming to conclude negotiations by the end of 2026, with negotiators holding monthly meetings since January. /mr For comprehensive coverage, in-depth analysis, visit our special page for West Philippine Sea updates . Stay informed with articles, videos, and expert opinions",
