   "url": "https://leadership.ng/full-list-us-warns-citizens-against-travelling-to-23-countries/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:48:25 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794322105.0,
   "ageDays": 1.38,
   "summary": "The countries affected include Afghanistan, Belarus, Burkina Faso, Burma, the Central African Republic, Chad, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Haiti, Iran, Iraq, Lebanon, Libya, Mali, Niger, North Korea, Russia, Somalia, South Sudan, Sudan, Syria, Uganda, Ukraine and Yemen.",
   "summary_zh": "受影响的国家包括阿富汗、白俄罗斯、布基纳法索、缅甸、中非共和国、乍得、刚果民主共和国、海地、伊朗、伊拉克、黎巴嫩、利比亚、马里、尼日尔、朝鲜、俄罗斯、索马里、南苏丹、苏丹、叙利亚、乌干达、乌克兰和也门。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The countries affected include Afghanistan, Belarus, Burkina Faso, Burma, the Central African Republic, Chad, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Haiti, Iran, Iraq, Lebanon, Libya, Mali, Niger, North Korea, Russia, Somalia, South Sudan, Sudan, Syria, Uganda, Ukraine and Yemen. The warning was issued by the department’s Bureau of Consular Affairs in a post on its official Facebook page on Monday, citing security concerns, prevailing local conditions and the US government’s limited capacity to provide assistance to its citizens in the affected countries. Explaining the classification, the department said Level 4 advisories were reserved for destinations considered dangerous, urging Americans to avoid travelling to the countries regardless of the circumstances. “Level 4 means DO NOT TRAVEL. We assign Level 4 based on local conditions and/or our limited ability to help Americans there. These places are dangerous. Do not go for ANY reason,” the department stated. The US Department of State operates a four-tier travel advisory system to guide American citizens planning international trips. Under the system, Level 1 advises travellers to exercise normal precautions, while Level 2 recommends increased caution because of potential risks. Level 3 urges Americans to reconsider their travel plans, while Level 4 represents the highest warning category, advising against all travel to the designated destinations. The department also urged Americans to consult its official travel advisory website for country-specific security updates and other relevant information before making international travel arrangements. Travellers can access the advisories through its website at travel.state.gov/destination. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates → Join Our WhatsApp Channel --> --> Leah Ndagi Leah Fatima Ndagi is a Content and Digital Journalist with Leadership Newspaper, bringing vast experience in social media management and three years of parliamentary reporting to her work. Her background spans digital content creation and legislative coverage, positioning her at the intersection of traditional journalism and modern digital storytelling",
