   "title": "Army temporarily grounds Apache helicopters amid US inspection for possible defect",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/defense/20261110/army-temporarily-grounds-apache-helicopters-amid-us-inspection-for-possible-defect",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:42:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794310923.0,
   "ageDays": 1.51,
   "summary": "The Korean Army has temporarily grounded its Apache military helicopters as U.S. authorities began inspections on the fleet over a possible malfunction of their transmission system, an Army official said Tuesday. The grounding of the AH-64E Apache Guardian attack helicopters has been in place since early October, after the Army received a safety advisory from the U.S. military regarding the transmission component, Army spokesperson Capt.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国陆军一名官员周二表示，随着美国有关部门开始检查其直升机机队，以排查传动系统可能出现的故障，韩国陆军已暂时停飞其阿帕奇军用直升机。自10月初收到美国军方针对传动部件的安全建议后，韩国陆军便停飞AH-64E“阿帕奇守护者”攻击直升机。陆军发言人上尉。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Korean Army has temporarily grounded its Apache military helicopters as U.S. authorities began inspections on the fleet over a possible malfunction of their transmission system, an Army official said Tuesday. The grounding of the AH-64E Apache Guardian attack helicopters has been in place since early October, after the Army received a safety advisory from the U.S. military regarding the transmission component, Army spokesperson Capt. Bae Seok-jin said in a press briefing. \"As a safety precaution, the Army temporarily grounded the fleet in early October (for the U.S. side) to conduct technical inspections in phases,\" Bae said. \"Operations will resume sequentially based on the inspection results.\" While routine training flights are paused during the grounding, the helicopters usually stand ready for an immediate operational launch in the event of a contingency. \"There are currently no issues with our readiness or operational posture,\" the Army spokesperson added. Manufactured by Boeing, the Apache helicopters serve as a key asset for air-to-ground defense for the Korean military, which currently operates a fleet of 36 units. The U.S. Army issued a statement early last month on the temporary pause of flight operations for Apache helicopters, citing technical assessments of their transmission systems. The inspections follow an August crash of an Apache helicopter in Texas that killed two U.S. soldiers. The same model also went down during a patrol operation near the Strait of Hormuz in June for reasons that have not been identified. Other countries operating the Apache chopper appear to be taking the same step. Taiwan also grounded the helicopters last month, local media have reported",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
