   "title": "Russia and Ukraine Begin New Round of U.S.-Mediated Peace Talks in Abu Dhabi",
   "url": "https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2026/11/10/russia-and-ukraine-begin-new-round-of-us-mediated-peace-talks-in-abu-dhabi-a94216",
   "domain": "themoscowtimes.com",
   "source": "themoscowtimes.com",
   "published": "Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:35:00 +0300",
   "_dt": 1794299700.0,
   "ageDays": 1.64,
   "summary": "Russian and Ukrainian delegates have gathered in Abu Dhabi on Tuesday for a new round of U.S.-mediated peace talks, though expectations for a breakthrough remain low as Russia appears determined to continue fighting rather than negotiate a settlement to the war, now in its fifth year. Delegates from Russia and Ukraine last met in Geneva in February, though negotiations were put on hold following the outbreak of the U.S. Israel war against Iran.",
   "summary_zh": "俄罗斯和乌克兰代表于周二聚集在阿布扎比，参加新一轮由美国斡旋的和平会谈；不过，随着战争进入第五个年头，俄罗斯似乎决心继续战斗，而不是通过谈判达成和平解决协议，因此各方对取得突破的预期仍然较低。俄罗斯和乌克兰代表去年2月在日内瓦举行会谈，但美国以色列对伊朗的战争爆发后，谈判一度中止。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Russian and Ukrainian delegates have gathered in Abu Dhabi on Tuesday for a new round of U.S.-mediated peace talks, though expectations for a breakthrough remain low as Russia appears determined to continue fighting rather than negotiate a settlement to the war, now in its fifth year. White House special envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner are once again mediating the talks, which last through Wednesday. Both men have held a series of meetings with officials across Europe and Russia in recent weeks as they engage in a renewed charge of shuttle diplomacy. Delegates from Russia and Ukraine last met in Geneva in February, though negotiations were put on hold following the outbreak of the U.S. Israel war against Iran. Since then, Ukraine and Russia have dramatically ramped up their attacks on each other ’s territory, inflicting significant economic pain and a growing human toll. Kremlin adviser Vladimir Medinsky, an arch-conservative who previously served as Russia’s culture minister, is again serving as the chief negotiator of the Russian delegation. The team also includes senior military and intelligence officials. The primary focus of the latest round of negotiations, Umerov wrote , includes a “cessation of hostilities, reliable post-war security guarantees, Ukraine’s economic recovery and development, as well as humanitarian steps. ” A source in Russia’s delegation told Reuters that Moscow hopes the Abu Dhabi talks will lay the groundwork for key elements of a post-war security framework for Europe. U.S. officials also told the Financial Times that they are looking to resolve the Ukraine war and broader security arrangements for the continent in tandem, but emphasized that European officials should have a seat at the table, something that Moscow has so far rejected . This is a breaking news story. Please come back later for more details. We are facing unprecedented challenges. Russia's Prosecutor General's Office has designated The Moscow Times as an \"undesirable\" organization, criminalizing our work and putting our staff at risk of prosecution. This follows our earlier unjust labeling as a \"foreign agent.\" These actions are direct attempts to silence independent journalism in Russia. The authorities claim our work \"discredits the decisions of the Russian leadership.\" We see things differently: we strive to provide accurate, unbiased reporting on Russia. We, the journalists of The Moscow Times, refuse to be silenced. But to continue our work, we need your help . Your support, no matter how small, makes a world of difference. If you can, please support us monthly starting from just $ 2. It's quick to set up, and every contribution makes a significant impact. By supporting The Moscow Times, you're defending open, independent journalism in the face of repression. Thank you for standing with us",
